# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked, not ignored (N5): this repo ships an
# application (gist-ffi -> xcframework -> app), so a committed lockfile gives
# reproducible builds and is what cargo-deny's checks rely on. This entry
# used to say the opposite of what the repo actually does — corrected rather
# than left standing. (fuzz/Cargo.lock is separately tracked too, for the
# same reason — cargo-fuzz targets keep their own lockfile outside the root
# workspace; see fuzz/Cargo.toml's `[workspace]` note.)

# Xcode — project file is generated by XcodeGen, never committed
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
# uniffi-generated Swift — built by Xcode build phase
apps/apple/Generated/
DerivedData/
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.dmg

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Build artifacts
artifacts/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (transient, per-session)
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
